The CEDFrequencyMerger and CEDTemporalMapper definitions and initialization
are retained from Mizar runtime/stage1/models/ced.py. The CED encoder model
code and weights are separate remote assets and retain their own terms.

This isolated training runtime is copied from mizar_l14_17x3_strong_reason,
with standard models copied from the existing official CED training route.
It strictly inherits the complete official final Mizar checkpoint and retains
all 30 physical text layers, executing each exactly once. The entire mapper
and LM train; the CED backbone stays frozen in eval mode. No parameters are added.
Online decoding/staging, eight-GPU microbatch-four with up to four-step
gradient accumulation, and complete-state checkpoints retain the reference
training semantics of the established reference runtime. The S3 half-epoch
budget, tokenizer/layout and full-model training are local adaptations.
Copied parent source identities are recorded in parent_sources.json.
